271
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:51,170
-(SINGING) What's the
 story, morning glory?

272
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:53,110
What's the word, hummingbird?

273
00:07:53,110 --> 00:07:54,490
Did you kiss him and cry?

274
00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:56,320
---Taylor.

275
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,070
NARRATOR: You a cheat, John?

276
00:07:58,070 --> 00:07:58,840
-Huh.

277
00:07:58,840 --> 00:08:00,740
NARRATOR: John,
 what have you done?

278
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:01,730
-Mother Teresa called.

279
00:08:01,730 --> 00:08:02,320
She hates you.

280
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:05,210
NARRATOR: Remember how it all
 started, the day you went over

281
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:06,750
to Mary's house
 to study the test.

282
00:08:06,750 --> 00:08:07,680
-Oh.

283
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:08,550
NARRATOR: Remember?

284
00:08:08,550 --> 00:08:10,930
-There are not enough bell
 towers in the world for Johnny.

285
00:08:10,930 --> 00:08:11,500
-All right, John.

286
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,010
Now look.

287
00:08:12,010 --> 00:08:16,690
The problem is to factor x
 squared minus 9x plus 20.

288
00:08:16,690 --> 00:08:17,760
Now how do you do it?

289
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:18,330
-I can't do it.

290
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:19,540
-Oh, let's just cheat.

291
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,570
-x squared minus 9x plus 20.

292
00:08:22,570 --> 00:08:25,880
You take the x squared
 minus the 9x and--

293
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:26,570
-Uh-uh.

294
00:08:26,570 --> 00:08:27,810
Nobody home, huh?

295
00:08:27,810 --> 00:08:30,620
-Oh, you subtract x from
 x squared, and then you--

296
00:08:30,620 --> 00:08:32,250
-(FEMALE VOICE) John,
 this is geography.

297
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:33,350
-Aw, golly, Mary.

298
00:08:33,350 --> 00:08:35,980
I don't know anything about
 this factoring business.

299
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:37,290
-John, you do too.

300
00:08:37,290 --> 00:08:37,790
-Woah.

301
00:08:37,790 --> 00:08:39,730
-Now the answer
 is the quantity x

302
00:08:39,730 --> 00:08:42,950
minus 5 times the
 quantity x minus 4.

303
00:08:42,950 --> 00:08:43,750
-(WHISPERING) Of course.

304
00:08:43,750 --> 00:08:44,950
-Now do you see how I got it?

305
00:08:44,950 --> 00:08:46,410
-Yeah, I guess I do.

306
00:08:46,410 --> 00:08:48,690
But golly, Mary,
 this stuff's awful.

307
00:08:48,690 --> 00:08:50,610
I just don't get most of it.

308
00:08:50,610 --> 00:08:54,090
-You'll just have to or you
 won't pass the test tomorrow.

309
00:08:54,090 --> 00:08:56,160
-I know it.

310
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:56,660
Mary--

311
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:58,300
-Will you kill me?

312
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:01,300
---if I get stuck on the test,
 you'll help me, won't you?

313
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:01,790
-[GASPS]

314
00:09:01,790 --> 00:09:02,290
-[GASPS]

315
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:03,960
-How can I help you?

316
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,120
-It's easy.

317
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,550
Miss Granby hardly ever
 comes back to where we sit.

318
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:08,290
-Huh.

319
00:09:08,290 --> 00:09:11,280
-If I get stuck, I'll just
 ask you for the answer.

320
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:11,810
-Plot point.

321
00:09:11,810 --> 00:09:13,160
-Well, I don't know.

322
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:13,960
-Oh, forget it.

323
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,690
I probably won't have
 any trouble anyway.

324
00:09:15,690 --> 00:09:16,500
-[MOCKING_LAUGH]

325
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,160
-Boobie.

326
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:20,140
NARRATOR: But you remember what
 happened the next day, John.

327
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:21,120
-You commited a mortal sin.

328
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:22,620
NARRATOR: Miss Granby's
 test was even tougher

329
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,170
than you thought it would be.

330
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:24,670
-[GROANS]

331
00:09:24,670 --> 00:09:26,830
NARRATOR: There were a lot of
 problems you couldn't work.

332
00:09:26,830 --> 00:09:27,510
-[GROANS]

333
00:09:27,510 --> 00:09:29,400
NARRATOR: And it seemed
 to you that you didn't

334
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:30,290
stand a chance--

335
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:31,090
-Stop it.

336
00:09:31,090 --> 00:09:32,510
Stop the voices in my head.

337
00:09:32,510 --> 00:09:33,010
[GROANS]

338
00:09:33,010 --> 00:09:34,380
NARRATOR: And right
 there in front of you

339
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:37,120
sat your pal, Mary,
 with her head chock

340
00:09:37,120 --> 00:09:38,940
full of all the
 answers you needed.

341
00:09:38,940 --> 00:09:40,320
-Split it open now.

342
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:42,160
NARRATOR: You thought about it.

343
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:44,970
There you were,
 desperate, and there

344
00:09:44,970 --> 00:09:47,620
was your salvation
 within arm's reach.

345
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:48,800
-On a doily.

346
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,910
NARRATOR: So you decided
 to take a chance.

347
00:09:50,910 --> 00:09:51,410
-(LOUDLY) Psst.

348
00:09:51,410 --> 00:09:53,020
Hey, Mary, what's the answer?

349
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:54,590
NARRATOR: You asked
 Mary for help.

350
00:09:54,590 --> 00:09:58,640
And of course, Mary, being
 Mary, gave you the help.

351
00:09:58,640 --> 00:09:59,830
-Sweet Mary, no!

352
00:09:59,830 --> 00:10:00,330
Don't.

353
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:02,750
NARRATOR: It was all so simple.

354
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:05,200
You began to wonder why
 you spent so much time

355
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:06,620
worrying about the test.

356
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:07,140
-Huh.

357
00:10:07,140 --> 00:10:07,770
NARRATOR: Yes, sir.

358
00:10:07,770 --> 00:10:09,710
You felt pretty
 pleased with yourself.

359
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:10,480
-Yeah.

360
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,720
NARRATOR: You'd put one over--

361
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:14,150
NARRATOR: --on Miss Granby.

362
00:10:14,150 --> 00:10:18,660
A few days later, Miss Granby
 returned the graded papers.

363
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:21,500
-Your one mistake, you signed
 your test Mary Matthews.

364
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,440
Oops.

365
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:25,170
-(FEMALE VOICE) This contract
 arrived for you from a Mr.

366
00:10:25,170 --> 00:10:26,550
Elzebub.

367
00:10:26,550 --> 00:10:29,350
-For the first time,
 Johnny feels real power.

368
00:10:29,350 --> 00:10:32,050
NARRATOR: Was there a shadow
 of doubt in Miss Granby's face

369
00:10:32,050 --> 00:10:33,010
as she looked at you?

370
00:10:33,010 --> 00:10:34,200
-Or was it lust?

371
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,620
NARRATOR: What was there
 for Miss Granby to doubt?

372
00:10:36,620 --> 00:10:38,330
After all, wasn't
 this the best grade

373
00:10:38,330 --> 00:10:40,140
you'd ever made on
 an algebra test?

374
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:40,740
-Well-- [CHUCKLES]

375
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:41,870
NARRATOR: Maybe that was it.

376
00:10:41,870 --> 00:10:42,370
-Hmm.

377
00:10:42,370 --> 00:10:43,680
NARRATOR: Maybe the
 grade was too good.

378
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,180
-Hmm.

379
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:44,970
-Mm.

380
00:10:44,970 --> 00:10:46,830
NARRATOR: Somehow that
 odd little look Miss

381
00:10:46,830 --> 00:10:50,230
Granby gave you
 seemed to harm you.

382
00:10:50,230 --> 00:10:51,060
-Did you really--

383
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:51,560
-Ow.

384
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,160
---earn that--

385
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:56,280
-Hi, Miss Granby.
 [GASPS] [YELLING]

386
00:10:56,280 --> 00:10:58,610
JOHN NARRATING: Aw, she
 didn't mean anything.

387
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:01,080
That test wasn't very
 important anyway.

388
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:02,540
-Yeah, just keep
 telling yourself that.

389
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:04,990
NARRATOR: Yes, you thought
 it was just a little thing,

390
00:11:04,990 --> 00:11:07,680
but it was the beginning
 of all your troubles.

391
00:11:07,680 --> 00:11:09,000
-(ITALIAN ACCENT)
 You talking to me?

392
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:09,500
Hey.

393
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,990
NARRATOR: After that,
 life went on for you

394
00:11:10,990 --> 00:11:12,420
pretty much as usual.

395
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,580
You were busier than
 ever with sports--

396
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,480
-Shaving points

397
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,640
---with Mary and
 your friend Jim,

398
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:20,170
and most of all with your new
 job as the student council

399
00:11:20,170 --> 00:11:20,670
representative.

400
00:11:20,670 --> 00:11:22,100
-I envision a cheating wing.

401
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:24,440
NARRATOR: You'd always wanted
 to be on the student council.

402
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:26,570
And you were really
 proud of yourself the day

403
00:11:26,570 --> 00:11:28,270
you were elected to
 take Jack Martin's

404
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:30,200
place when he moved out of town.

405
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:31,520
-Under mysterious circumstances.

406
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:33,730
NARRATOR: But now with
 the honor of the job

407
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:35,830
went the necessity of
 keeping your grades up.

408
00:11:35,830 --> 00:11:37,140
-And your enemies down.

409
00:11:37,140 --> 00:11:38,340
NARRATOR: And that
 was your problem.

410
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:39,060
-Dear Joe McGinniss--

411
00:11:39,060 --> 00:11:39,660
[TELEPHONE RINGING

412
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:41,080
---I admire-- Uh-oh.

413
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,920
Oh, oh.

414
00:11:43,920 --> 00:11:45,350
-Maybe he'd do better
 if he had parents.

415
00:11:45,350 --> 00:11:46,190
-Yeah.

416
00:11:46,190 --> 00:11:47,550
-[CHUCKLES

417
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:48,050
-Hello?

418
00:11:48,050 --> 00:11:49,120
JIM (ON TELEPHONE): This is Jim.

419
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,000
-In the next room?

420
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,660
JIM (ON TELEPHONE): Let's
 go down to Sam's and get

421
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:52,160
a hamburger.

422
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:52,840
-I can't, Jim.

423
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,560
I've got homework to do.

424
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,270
JIM (ON TELEPHONE): Oh,
 don't worry about it.

425
00:11:56,270 --> 00:11:58,670
You've got plenty of time.

426
00:11:58,670 --> 00:12:01,190
-(FEMALE VOICE) I will
 bring you down, Johnny.

427
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:01,690
-OK.

428
00:12:01,690 --> 00:12:02,800
Let's go get a hamburger.

429
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:04,530
I'll see you in a minute.

430
00:12:04,530 --> 00:12:06,810
-Now was this Ingmar
 Bergman's first American film?

431
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:09,450
-[CHUCKLES] I think.

432
00:12:09,450 --> 00:12:10,800
NARRATOR: The big
 clock in the hall

433
00:12:10,800 --> 00:12:14,630
went on ticking off its
 even measure of time.

434
00:12:14,630 --> 00:12:16,070
And you went on as before.

435
00:12:16,070 --> 00:12:17,200
-Shh.

436
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,300
-Eating hamburgers
 while the world cried.

437
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:21,370
NARRATOR: You and Mary were
 still the best of friends.

438
00:12:21,370 --> 00:12:24,340
But Mary had assumed
 greater importance to you.

439
00:12:24,340 --> 00:12:27,450
You came to depend upon her
 more and more in your school

440
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:29,850
work, although you
 scarcely realized it.

441
00:12:29,850 --> 00:12:31,100
-You worked her
 like a punch press--

442
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:31,900
NARRATOR: It wasn't--
 ---Johnny.

443
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:34,090
NARRATOR: --that Mary was
 any smarter than you were.

444
00:12:34,090 --> 00:12:37,390
It was just, well, that she
 seemed to find more time--

445
00:12:37,390 --> 00:12:38,060
-Well.
 NARRATOR: --to study.

446
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:38,560
-Well.

447
00:12:38,560 --> 00:12:40,440
NARRATOR: And you were
 student council representative

448
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:43,350
and a very busy fellow.

449
00:12:43,350 --> 00:12:44,410
-You've gotta help me.

450
00:12:44,410 --> 00:12:46,090
What's the answer
 to number nine?

451
00:12:46,090 --> 00:12:47,820
-Shh.

452
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:48,320
-[SIGHS]

453
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:49,700
-(FEMALE VOICE) I
 smell a big commie rat.

454
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:52,860
-John--

455
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:53,360
-Oh.

456
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:53,860
[GASPS]

457
00:12:53,860 --> 00:12:55,210
---bring it up here, please.

458
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:55,940
-[MAKING_BUZZER_SOUND]

459
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:56,740
-Ding, ding, ding, ding.

460
00:12:56,740 --> 00:13:01,660
-Put your pencil down, and
 step away from your desk.

461
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:02,790
-(MIMICKING NARRATOR)
 Fortunately,

462
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:06,830
your mob ties will
 get you off, Johnny.

463
00:13:06,830 --> 00:13:08,370
-(FEMALE VOICE) Gimme that.

464
00:13:08,370 --> 00:13:08,870
Wow.

465
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:09,980
That's randy.

466
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:13,160
-I'm afraid I'll have to give
 you both zero on the test.

467
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:13,660
-[GASPS]

468
00:13:13,660 --> 00:13:14,810
-Ja wohl, mein Fuhrer.

469
00:13:14,810 --> 00:13:17,690
-And both of you are to report
 to me after school, please.

470
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:18,190
-[GASPS]

471
00:13:18,190 --> 00:13:19,490
-Ohh.

472
00:13:19,490 --> 00:13:21,740
-And so Dana Plato's
 career began.

473
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:23,740
NARRATOR: So you
 were caught, John.

474
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:26,200
You were exposed in
 front of the class.

475
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:28,680
And what's more, Mary
 was involved too,

476
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:30,560
Mary, who was only
 trying to help.

477
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,490
-(MIMICKING NARRATORY) Mary,
 who'll have to take the fall.

478
00:13:32,490 --> 00:13:33,720
NARRATOR: And then
 what happened?

479
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:34,360
-Spare some change?

480
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:37,330
NARRATOR: Your classmates seemed
 to treat you a little coldly.

481
00:13:37,330 --> 00:13:39,640
Perhaps it was because they
 had studied and worked hard

482
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:40,560
for their grades.

483
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,540
-Yeah.

484
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,800
NARRATOR: Maybe they felt
 that your cheating gave you

485
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,330
an unfair advantage.

486
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:46,140
-I belong in hell.

487
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:47,410
NARRATOR: And their
 thoughts about you

488
00:13:47,410 --> 00:13:49,460
were reflected in another way.

489
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,720
-(WHISPERING) Pig.

490
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,750
-Hey, what's up?

491
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:53,090
-Meeting of the student council.

492
00:13:53,090 --> 00:13:54,720
-(SOUTHERN ACCENT) They're
 hanging you in effigy.

493
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,630
-That's funny.

494
00:13:55,630 --> 00:13:56,930
My name isn't on there.

495
00:13:56,930 --> 00:13:59,080
I'm on student council.

496
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,030
-I don't think you'd want
 to come to this meeting.

497
00:14:01,030 --> 00:14:01,800
It's about you.

498
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:02,300
-[CHUCKLES]

499
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:02,800
-Me?

500
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,680
-That's what I hear.

501
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:05,700
-(SOUTHERN ACCENT) By the
 way, have you seen my ribcage?

502
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:06,200
-[CHUCKLES]

503
00:14:06,200 --> 00:14:08,250
-Say, would you mind calling
 me after the meeting's over,

504
00:14:08,250 --> 00:14:10,200
and let me know
 how it comes out?

505
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:10,900
-No, I wouldn't mind.

506
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:12,070
-(SOUTHERN ACCENT)
 We really should

507
00:14:12,070 --> 00:14:13,520
be talking through our lawyers.

508
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:16,010
-No, I don't say that
 what John did was right.

509
00:14:16,010 --> 00:14:17,820
But I do think we ought to
 give him another chance.

510
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:19,120
-You mean you think
 we ought to let

511
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,900
him go on being in
 the student council?

512
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:21,670
-I think we should.

513
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:22,170
-I don't.

514
00:14:22,170 --> 00:14:23,420
-Will the senator yield?

515
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,370
---a good representative.

516
00:14:24,370 --> 00:14:24,870
-That's right.

517
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:27,120
But I don't think anyone that
 cheats should hold an office.

518
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:27,620
-That's right.

519
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:29,930
I think we should elect
 a new representative.

520
00:14:29,930 --> 00:14:31,310
[ALL ARGUING]

521
00:14:31,310 --> 00:14:32,000
-All right.

522
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:32,650
Wait a minute.

523
00:14:32,650 --> 00:14:33,150
Wait a minute.

524
00:14:33,150 --> 00:14:35,170
We won't get anywhere
 by all talking at once.

525
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:36,900
Are we ready to take a vote now?

526
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:37,870
-Margaret Chase Smith.

527
00:14:37,870 --> 00:14:40,380
-All in favor of giving
 John another chance,

528
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:41,780
hold up your hand.

529
00:14:41,780 --> 00:14:42,280
-Woah.

530
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:44,940
-All who think we should
 elect a new student council

531
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:46,090
representative,
 hold up your hand.

532
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:46,590
-Oh.

